{
 "title": "United in Currency, Divided in Growth: Dynamic Effects of Euro Adoption",
 "hypothesis": "Euro adoption reduced long-run annual GDP growth; heterogeneity by initial GDP per capita and other pre-treatment characteristics.",
 "data_sources": [
  "Penn World Tables 10.0 (rgdpe/pop)",
  "World Bank WDI"
 ],
 "sample": "Unbalanced panel 35 countries 1970-2023: 20 eurozone treatment (11 founders 1999: AT,BE,FI,FR,DE,IE,IT,LU,NL,PT,ES plus GR 2001, SI 2007, CY/MT 2008, SK 2009, EE 2011, LV 2014, LT 2015, HR 2023) and 15 never-treated controls (DK,SE,UK + AU,CA,IS,IL,JP,KR,NZ,NO,CH,US). Appendix robustness EU-only controls DK,SE,UK. Pre-treatment characteristics measured 1998 or year before adoption.",
 "period_start": "1970",
 "period_end": "2023",
 "method": [
  "1. Sample: 35 countries 1970-2023, ~2,010 country-year obs. Treatment D_it=1 if i adopted euro by t (founders 1999, later adopters respective year). Event time k_it = t - T_i_euro, k∈[-10,20] main([-5,20] shown).",
  "2. Outcome Y_it = log-difference real GDP per capita (PWT expenditure-side rgdpe/pop). Mechanism outcomes: consumption growth, investment growth, net exports/GDP, labor productivity (output/worker) and TFP rtfpna, current account.",
  "3. Features X_i pre-treatment (1998 or year before adoption): initial GDP per capita (2017$), trade openness (X+M/GDP), investment share, human capital index; standardized.",
  "4. CFFE: causal forest with two-way fixed effects residualized within each node: Y~ - alpha_i - gamma_t, D~ - pi_i - rho_t on node ℓ observations. Feature vector ~X_it=(k_it,X_i). Model Y_it=alpha_i+gamma_t+tau(k_it,X_i)*D_it+eps. n_trees=500 baseline (200 in stability), min_leaf=30, honesty enabled, node-level FE.",
  "5. Dynamic ATT(k)=1/N_k sum_{i:k_it=k} tau_hat(k,X_i). Cluster-robust var: 1/N_k^2 sum_i (sum_{t:k_it=k}(tau_hat_it - tau_hat(k)))^2. Plus block bootstrap 200 reps resampling country time series.",
  "6. Classical benchmark: Y_it=alpha_i+gamma_t+sum_{k=-10}^{20} beta_k 1[k_it=k]+eps, k=-1 ref, country-clustered SE. Alternatives: Sun-Abraham (2021) interaction-weighted, Callaway-SantAnna (2021) doubly-robust, Bai (2009) interactive FE lamda_i'f_t.",
  "7. Robustness: EU-only controls, excl crisis 2008-2015, pre-crisis k<9 vs crisis+ k>=9, placebo fake dates 1995/1997 to adopters, placebo 1999 to DK/SE/UK, leave-one-out, hyperparameter/time/anticipation/sample splits."
 ],
